# A line of only whitespace, shorter than the closing delimiter's indentation, reads
# as an empty line: it holds no text that could be under-indented. An editor that
# trims trailing whitespace makes it truly empty, and that is already accepted.
#= {result: 'x\n\ny', known_issue: 'FROST-151'}
def text = '''
    x
  
    y
    '''
text
